                    {
                        "sense_id": "af99a148-9074-3c26-ba9f-2d88eb1ba731",
                        "entry_id": "73e9dbbb-7626-3a2b-96de-05d8e72f75ec",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Drawing out or lengthening in time; prolonging; continuing or delaying."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "efa8253c-1aa7-4961-805b-22546b7713e8",
                                "sense_id": "af99a148-9074-3c26-ba9f-2d88eb1ba731",
                                "text": "He suffered their protractive arts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce6b3f78-2fa6-42ba-85b4-b357763ca4f1",
                                "sense_id": "af99a148-9074-3c26-ba9f-2d88eb1ba731",
                                "text": "In this case one half of the group had a contractive distraction imposed (decreasing work time) by a confederate; the other a protractive distraction (increasing work time)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f0fea01-0810-4e1a-82fd-794bb57dbe33",
                                "sense_id": "af99a148-9074-3c26-ba9f-2d88eb1ba731",
                                "text": "Such a function could only be used in the protractive approach to evaluate different states of the system , for it does not necessarily specify an established point of convergency ."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b0298165-f1a4-3926-8d2d-02d74d21b041",
                        "entry_id": "73e9dbbb-7626-3a2b-96de-05d8e72f75ec",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Indicating an action or state that is ongoing or sustained."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0bb537c7-4e59-45a0-8639-14a731995c82",
                                "sense_id": "b0298165-f1a4-3926-8d2d-02d74d21b041",
                                "text": "One inflected form of the durative verb is made with a long tense hold and without motion; the nuance in meaning is the same as that of the protractive modulation of adjectival predicates and translates as 'to stare at (uninterruptedly)' (figure 12.15b)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "70630687-a837-487e-b95f-2e151ffed324",
                                "sense_id": "b0298165-f1a4-3926-8d2d-02d74d21b041",
                                "text": "The protractive, durational, and continuative morphemes are examples of nonpunctual modifications ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f361d41-d7db-43be-a481-8c367ebbc492",
                                "sense_id": "b0298165-f1a4-3926-8d2d-02d74d21b041",
                                "text": "Fleischmann (1990:22), Sebastian and Slobin (1994: 257-8) also discuss the classivication of so-called aspectual verbs into inchative verbs (e.g. empezar, to start), protractive verbs ( e.g. , quedarse, to remain), cumulative verbs ( e.g., continuar, to continue) and and empletive verbs (e.g. acabar de, to finish).."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8aac5068-2aa3-3a38-bca6-4efd0ed4d9cc",
                        "entry_id": "73e9dbbb-7626-3a2b-96de-05d8e72f75ec",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Extending forward or projecting outward."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "99a63295-ae47-451a-b593-631ffaaed164",
                                "sense_id": "8aac5068-2aa3-3a38-bca6-4efd0ed4d9cc",
                                "text": "Axial ribs not strongly protractive."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1052efd4-c7a9-409c-8bc6-e0c294ae1583",
                                "sense_id": "8aac5068-2aa3-3a38-bca6-4efd0ed4d9cc",
                                "text": "This keel on the first half of the last whorl consists of oblique, protractive strong short ridges, which on the last half disappear and give place to rough corrugations."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1fe3ad5f-1a4a-44ef-90a3-07edc7e402b4",
                                "sense_id": "8aac5068-2aa3-3a38-bca6-4efd0ed4d9cc",
                                "text": "The horizontal component of the resultant muscular force is protractive during the closing stages,"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
